# Security and RLS

- Enable RLS on every exposed table. Define explicit SELECT, INSERT, UPDATE, and,
  where deletion is allowed, DELETE policies.
- Never bypass or disable RLS to make a feature work. Privileged bypass is limited
  to narrowly justified server administration.
- Enforce platform, school, club, and user scope in database policies; UI checks
  are not authorization.
- Resolve roles from persisted memberships and assignments. Never hard-code roles
  or authorize solely from `profiles.role`.
- Validate mutations with Zod, authenticate, authorize server-side, mutate, audit
  when relevant, and return a typed result.
- Use CSRF-safe mutations, secure headers/CSP, output escaping, abuse rate limits,
  recipient allow-listing, and protected asset URLs.
- Test both ALLOW and DENY cases, including cross-tenant access.
